The Story
In ancient Magadha, the Buddha was invited by the brahmin Wugou Miaoguang. On the road to his house, at a place called Fengcai — 丰财, Abundant Wealth — there was an old garden with a ruined, collapsed stupa, buried in weeds, become a heap of earth. To every passerby, it looked like an ordinary dirt mound.

When the Buddha arrived, the mound suddenly blazed with light. A voice in the void praised: "Excellent! Excellent! Shakyamuni Buddha, how supreme is your conduct today!"

The Buddha circumambulated the mound three times — 绕塔三匝 — covered it with his own robe — 脱衣覆盖 — wept, then smiled.

Vajrapani and the assembly asked: Why weep and smile at ordinary dirt?

The Buddha replied: This is not ordinary dirt. This is the whole-body relic stupa of countless Buddhas of the past.

